# --- Rust ---
target/
# Cargo.lock is committed because core-rs ships a binary (trustlayer-guardian);
# pin transitive deps for reproducible builds.

# --- Editors / OS / AI tooling ---
.idea/
.vscode/
# Ignore .claude/ contents — but NOT the directory itself, because git cannot
# re-include anything inside an excluded directory, and the skill symlinks
# below have to be tracked.
#
# ADR-023 §7 makes `.claude/skills/<name>` a symlink to the canonical
# `.opencode/skills/<name>` so Claude Code and OpenCode read one file and
# cannot drift. Ignoring them made that true only on the machine that created
# them: a fresh clone got the OpenCode copies and nothing for Claude Code —
# precisely the drift the ADR exists to prevent. Settings stay ignored; they
# are machine-local.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- TrustLayer scratch & runtime state ---
.temp_research/
obsidian_vault/.hermes_state/
.gitnexus/
examples/.demo_traces.jsonl
# Default JSONL trace-store log written when running the guardian from core-rs/.
events.jsonl
*.jsonl.compacting
core-rs/events.jsonl
# Art. 12 evidence sidecars (ADR-017). Traces carry prompts, responses and
# potentially personal data; none of it belongs in a public repository.
*.jsonl.chain
*.archive.jsonl
*.checkpoints.jsonl

# Ed25519 checkpoint signing keys. A committed signing key is a signing key
# that no longer signs anything meaningful — rotate immediately if one lands.
*.signing.key
signing.key
trustlayer-signing-*

# Compliance scan output. Regenerated on demand and, for third-party projects,
# potentially confidential.
readiness.json
remediation.md
compliance-report.json
.routekit/
.verify-venv/
